     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:review_status "PENDING" ;
     se:scope_description "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a Chapter 2 sections 2.4 and 3 (printed pages 2-7 to 2-9); generally accepted KA content, not a mandated documentation procedure." ;
     se:statement "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a KA2 frames architectural design as producing a network of significant decisions whose quality-attribute trade-offs and rationale can be recorded, and warns that deferred decisions can accumulate architectural technical debt borne by later work." .

se:CLM-ARC-SWEBOK-DESCRIPTION-DISTINCTION a se:KnowledgeClaim ;
     se:SUPPORTED_BY se:EVD-ARC-SWEBOK-DESCRIPTION-VIEWS ;
     se:applicability "Professional-BOK grounding for the architecture-description boundary this lane previously had to leave as curriculum abstraction levels only; complements, and does not replace, the ISO/IEC/IEEE 42010 metadata-only record." ;
     se:claim_kind "DEFINITION" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-06" ;
     se:evidence_refs se:EVD-ARC-SWEBOK-DESCRIPTION-VIEWS ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PENDING_REVIEW" ;
     se:limitations "The Guide's authority limitations apply: a guide to generally accepted knowledge, not a uniform prescription; its citations are not comprehensive." ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:review_status "PENDING" ;
     se:scope_description "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a Chapter 2 section 2 (printed pages 2-4 to 2-7); generally accepted KA content, not a prescription of a mandatory viewpoint set." ;
     se:statement "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a KA2 distinguishes a software system's architecture from its architecture description, and characterizes descriptions as stakeholder-addressed work products commonly organized as multiple views whose conventions are documented as viewpoints, with architectural styles and patterns as documented solution forms and reference architectures as architectures that constrain or guide other architectures and provide a common basis for further architectural development." .

se:CLM-ARC-SWEBOK-DESIGN-STAGE-SPLIT a se:KnowledgeClaim ;
     se:SUPPORTED_BY se:EVD-ARC-SWEBOK-DESIGN-STAGES ;
     se:applicability "Professional-BOK counterpart to the CS2023 architectural-design/detailed-design abstraction-level distinction in this lane." ;
     se:claim_kind "TAXONOMY_STATEMENT" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-06" ;
     se:evidence_refs se:EVD-ARC-SWEBOK-DESIGN-STAGES ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PENDING_REVIEW" ;
     se:limitations "The decomposition is conceptual; projects may blend stages, and the Guide does not prescribe sequencing." ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:review_status "PENDING" ;
     se:scope_description "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a Chapter 3 sections 1-2 (printed pages 3-2 to 3-6); a conceptual stage decomposition, not a mandated stage-gate process." ;
     se:statement "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a KA3 decomposes software design into architectural, high-level (external-facing) and detailed (internal-facing) stages, with high-level design fixing component interaction and environment contracts within the architectural envelope and detailed design fixing internal module characteristics within the high-level constraints." .

se:CLM-REQ-ELICITATION-MULTI-SOURCE a se:KnowledgeClaim ;
