se:CLM-REQ-SWEBOK-ELICITATION-ACTIVE a se:KnowledgeClaim ;
     se:SUPPORTED_BY se:EVD-REQ-SWEBOK-ELICITATION ;
     se:applicability "Professional-BOK characterization of the elicitation activity; usable as the professional-counterpart anchor for the CS2023-scoped elicitation records in this lane." ;
     se:claim_kind "PRACTICE_CLAIM" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-06" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PENDING_REVIEW" ;
     se:limitations "The Guide's authority limitations apply: it is a guide to generally accepted knowledge, not a uniform prescription, and its technique citations are not comprehensive." ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:review_status "PENDING" ;
     se:scope_description "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a Chapter 1 section 2 (printed pages 1-6 to 1-7); a description of generally accepted KA content, not a prescription that every project apply every listed technique." ;
     se:statement "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a KA1 presents requirements elicitation as an active, multi-source activity whose goal is to surface candidate requirements and minimize incompleteness, drawing on identified stakeholder classes and non-person sources and on a surveyed set of elicitation techniques." .

se:CLM-REQ-SWEBOK-MANAGEMENT-AGREEMENT a se:KnowledgeClaim ;
     se:SUPPORTED_BY se:EVD-REQ-SWEBOK-CHANGE-SCOPE ;
     se:applicability "Professional-BOK counterpart to the change-expectation principle and evolution records in this lane." ;
     se:claim_kind "PRACTICE_CLAIM" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-06" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PENDING_REVIEW" ;
     se:limitations "The sections describe activities in plan-based and Agile life cycles without asserting one universal process shape." ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:review_status "PENDING" ;
     se:scope_description "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a Chapter 1 sections 6-7 (printed pages 1-16 to 1-19); generally accepted KA content, not a claim that every project instantiates every listed element." ;
     se:statement "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a KA1 frames requirements management as maintaining the agreed requirements over time through scrubbing, change control and scope matching, with practical considerations that prioritization weigh satisfaction and dissatisfaction, that tracing serve consistency accounting and impact analysis, and that volatility assessment inform change-tolerant design." .

se:CLM-REQ-SWEBOK-VALIDATION-TRIO a se:KnowledgeClaim ;
     se:SUPPORTED_BY se:EVD-REQ-SWEBOK-VALIDATION-METHODS ;
     se:applicability "Professional-BOK counterpart to the curriculum's prototyping-as-validation records in this lane." ;
     se:claim_kind "DEFINITION" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-06" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PENDING_REVIEW" ;
     se:limitations "The definition covers stated requirements as currently understood; it does not claim validation proves completeness." ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:review_status "PENDING" ;
     se:scope_description "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a Chapter 1 section 5 (printed pages 1-15 to 1-16); generally accepted KA content, not a mandate of all three methods on every project." ;
     se:statement "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a KA1 defines requirements validation as gaining confidence that the requirements represent stakeholders' true needs as currently understood, and characterizes it as typically using three methods: requirements reviews (preferably from multiple perspectives), simulation or execution of the specification, and prototyping." .

se:CLM-TVV-0001 a se:KnowledgeClaim ;
     se:APPLIES_TO se:NODE-CS2023-SE-VALIDATION ;
     se:SUPPORTED_BY se:EVD-TVV-0003 ;
     se:applicability "Use as the curriculum's canonical V&V distinction; not a professional-standard definition (SWEBOK hold, ISO 29119 metadata-only)." ;
     se:claim_kind "DEFINITION" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-06" ;
     se:evidence_refs se:EVD-TVV-0003 ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PENDING_REVIEW" ;
     se:limitations "The two-question formulation distinguishes conformance-checking from fitness-for-purpose; it does not imply that passing tests proves correctness or that validation equals acceptance." ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:review_status "PENDING" ;
     se:scope_description "CS2023 SE-Validation knowledge unit, CS Core topic 1 and CS Core learning outcome 2." ;
     se:statement "CS2023's SE-Validation unit defines verification and validation as two distinct questions — verification asks whether the thing is being built right, and validation asks whether the right thing was built — and its learning outcomes expect students to distinguish program validation from verification." .

se:CLM-TVV-0002 a se:KnowledgeClaim ;
     se:SUPPORTED_BY se:EVD-TVV-0004 ;
     se:applicability "Use when classifying test kinds by level; cite the specific list being used because the two lists differ." ;
     se:claim_kind "TAXONOMY_STATEMENT" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-06" ;
     se:evidence_refs se:EVD-TVV-0004 ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PENDING_REVIEW" ;
     se:limitations "The source does not reconcile the two lists; this claim preserves, rather than resolves, the difference." ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:review_status "PENDING" ;
     se:scope_description "CS2023 SE-Validation CS Core topic 4 versus CS Core illustrative learning outcome 4." ;
     se:statement "Within CS2023's SE-Validation unit, the CS Core test-kinds topic enumerates unit, integration, validation and system testing, while the corresponding learning outcome additionally names regression and acceptance in its comparison set, so the curriculum states its test-kind taxonomy differently in the two places." .

se:CLM-TVV-0003 a se:KnowledgeClaim ;
     se:SUPPORTED_BY se:EVD-TVV-0005 ;
     se:applicability "Use as a curriculum enumeration of why software is tested; not a claim of exhaustiveness across professional practice." ;
     se:claim_kind "PRACTICE_CLAIM" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-06" ;
     se:evidence_refs se:EVD-TVV-0005 ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PENDING_REVIEW" ;
     se:limitations "Curriculum enumeration; the SWEBOK KA5 objective taxonomy beyond the reinspected sections and the inaccessible ISO 29119-2 content mean no cross-source objective list is asserted." ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:review_status "PENDING" ;
     se:scope_description "CS2023 SE-Validation CS Core topic 3 (curriculum authority only)." ;
     se:statement "CS2023 lists five testing objectives in the SE-Validation unit: usability, reliability, conformance to specification, performance and security." .

se:CLM-TVV-0004 a se:KnowledgeClaim ;
     se:QUALIFIED_BY se:EVD-TVV-0015 ;
     se:SUPPORTED_BY se:EVD-TVV-0010 ;
     se:applicability "Applies as SSDF v1.1 recommendation content only: risk, cost, feasibility and applicability govern whether and how it is adopted, and the framework is not a checklist." ;
     se:claim_kind "PRACTICE_CLAIM" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-06" ;
     se:evidence_refs se:EVD-TVV-0010 ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PENDING_REVIEW" ;
     se:limitations "Executing the tests is presented as finding vulnerabilities, not as proving the software correct.", "Notional implementation examples (regression tests for reported vulnerabilities, fuzz testing) are explicitly neither required nor exhaustive.", "Table 1 task ordering does not imply implementation sequence or relative importance." ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:review_status "PENDING" ;
     se:scope_description "NIST SP 800-218 v1.1, Section 2 practice PW.8 and tasks PW.8.1-PW.8.2 (secure-development cross-cutting source)." ;
     se:statement "NIST SP 800-218 v1.1 recommends (task PW.8.1) first determining whether executable code testing should be performed to find vulnerabilities not identified by previous reviews, analysis or testing and, if so, which testing types to use, and (task PW.8.2) then scoping, designing, performing and documenting the testing while recording and triaging all discovered issues and recommended remediations in the development team's workflow or issue tracking system." .

se:CLM-TVV-0005 a se:KnowledgeClaim ;
     se:SUPPORTED_BY se:EVD-TVV-0011 ;
     se:applicability "Describes this framework's grouping only; not a universal vulnerability-management taxonomy." ;
     se:claim_kind "TAXONOMY_STATEMENT" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-06" ;
     se:evidence_refs se:EVD-TVV-0011 ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PENDING_REVIEW" ;
     se:limitations "Group structure does not imply a mandatory identify-then-remediate-then-analyze workflow sequence." ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:review_status "PENDING" ;
     se:scope_description "NIST SP 800-218 v1.1 Section 2, RV practice group." ;
     se:statement "NIST SP 800-218 v1.1 structures its Respond to Vulnerabilities group as three practices: ongoing identification and confirmation of vulnerabilities (RV.1, whose task RV.1.2 explicitly cross-references PW.7 and PW.8), risk-based assessment, prioritization and remediation (RV.2), and root-cause analysis of vulnerabilities (RV.3)." .

se:CLM-TVV-0006 a se:KnowledgeClaim ;
     se:SUPPORTED_BY se:EVD-TVV-0007 ;
     se:applicability "Use when planning or auditing test coverage; code coverage alone represents one of the three dimensions." ;
