     se:result "The definition and the four named technique families were confirmed for the practice record." ;
     se:source_locator_ref se:LOC-07B-SWEBOK-KA4-INTRO-FUNDAMENTALS ;
     se:statement "SWEBOK v4.0a KA4 section 1.3 defines constructing for verification as building software in such a way that faults can be readily found by the software engineers writing the software as well as by testers and users during independent testing and operational activities, and names four supporting technique families: following coding standards to support code reviews and unit testing, organizing code to support automated testing, restricting the use of complex or difficult-to-understand language structures, and recording software behaviors with logs." ;
     se:synthetic "false"^^xsd:boolean .

