     se:source_locator_ref se:LOC-07B-SWEBOK-KA4-INTRO-FUNDAMENTALS ;
     se:statement "SWEBOK v4.0a KA4 defines software construction as the detailed creation and maintenance of software through coding, verification, unit testing, integration testing and debugging; states the KA is linked to all other KAs but most strongly to Software Design (much design work is performed during construction) and Software Testing (engineers unit-test and integration-test throughout construction); and notes that boundaries among design, construction and testing, if any, vary depending on the software life cycle processes used in a project." ;
