     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:result "The security-engineering goal, the problem/situational analysis topics, the tradeoff factors and the KA Core analysis/design/attestation topics were confirmed." ;
     se:source_locator_ref se:LOC-07C-CS2023-SEC-ENGINEERING ;
     se:statement "The CS2023 SEC-Engineering unit sets the CS Core goal of building systems that remain dependable despite errors, accidents, or malicious adversaries, teaches problem analysis and situational analysis to address system security, and teaches engineering tradeoff analysis based on time, cost, risk tolerance, risk acceptance, return on investment and similar factors. Its KA Core topics add security design and engineering — including functional requirements, security subsystems, information protection, security testing, security assessment and evaluation — security analysis covering security requirements analysis, security controls analysis, threat analysis and vulnerability analysis, and attestation of software products with respect to their specification and adaptiveness." ;
     se:synthetic "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
     se:uncertainty "Printed page numbers of the SEC-Engineering topics were not independently confirmed; heading-anchored citation is used." .

