     se:method "Direct inspection of the official SWEBOK v4.0a PDF on 2026-11-07 at the verified page index; original paraphrase." ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:result "The prevention/tolerance duality, the access-control and cryptography fundamentals, and the threat-modeling-to-design path were confirmed." ;
     se:source_locator_ref se:LOC-07C-SWEBOK-KA13-SECURITY-DESIGN ;
     se:statement "SWEBOK v4.0a KA13 section 4.2 frames security design as concerning how to prevent unauthorized disclosure, creation, change, deletion or denial of access to information and other resources, and how to tolerate security-related attacks or violations by limiting damage, continuing service, speeding repair and recovery, and failing and recovering securely; it names access control a fundamental concept of security, notes that most controls build on cryptographic algorithms and cryptographic material like keys whose selection, creation, distribution and management must be chosen carefully, and describes threat modeling — illustrating how a system is being attacked — as the means by which developers specify a security design for the mitigation." ;
     se:synthetic "false"^^xsd:boolean .

