     se:source_locator_ref se:LOC-07D-CS2023-SE-RELIABILITY-KU ;
     se:statement "CS2023 teaches that software failures are caused by defects (bugs), so for high reliability the goal is to have minimum defects: by injecting fewer defects in the first place — through better training, education and planning — and by removing most of the injected defects, through testing, code review and similar approaches. A paired core topic covers the defect injection and removal cycle and different approaches for defect removal." ;
     se:synthetic "false"^^xsd:boolean .

