     se:method "Read the SE-Reliability unit topic list in the official Body of Knowledge full text obtained via a text-extraction service on 2026-11-07; heading-anchored KU locator inside the registry-verified SE section page span." ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:result "The unit's topic inventory and learning outcomes were confirmed for the taxonomy-node definition and for scoping which topics are core versus elective." ;
     se:source_locator_ref se:LOC-07D-CS2023-SE-RELIABILITY-KU ;
     se:statement "The CS2023 SE-Reliability knowledge unit comprises six KA Core topics (the reliability concept; identifying reliability requirements for different kinds of software; defects as the cause of failures and the minimum-defect goal; software reliability versus system reliability and failure behavior; the defect injection and removal cycle; and comparing the error-budget approach with the error-free approach) and five Non-core topics (software reliability models; fault tolerance techniques and models; software reliability engineering practices; dependent and independent failure domains; measurement-based analysis of software reliability). Its KA Core illustrative learning outcomes include determining the level of reliability a system requires, explaining the problems in achieving very high reliability, and understanding fault-minimization approaches applicable at each lifecycle stage." ;
     se:synthetic "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
     se:uncertainty "The KU subsection's printed page number was not independently confirmed; heading-anchored citation is used." .

