     se:method "Direct inspection of the official SWEBOK v4.0a PDF (SHA-256 0c9db4da0b2425c58cf778b99131eb31bb6c188e98b67163a549a1366d96e511) on 2026-11-07; text extracted at the verified page index and paraphrased originally." ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:result "The plan-early framing, the demand-driven infrastructure trend and the early-testing opportunity were confirmed for the professional-BOK scoped claim." ;
     se:source_locator_ref se:LOC-07D-SWEBOK-KA6-PERF-REL-LB ;
     se:statement "SWEBOK v4.0a KA6 section 1.6 states that software operations engineers plan for performance, reliability and load balancing early in software projects so that project requirements are met, cross-referencing the Software Requirements KA for those requirements. It observes a current trend of designing and using infrastructure/operations services that adjust the infrastructure dynamically (for example for scalability) according to demand, and notes that DevOps practices enable operations engineers to anticipate these needs early and to provide infrastructure services that software engineers can use and test during the development stages of a project." ;
     se:synthetic "false"^^xsd:boolean .

se:EVD-07D-SWEBOK-RELIABILITY-MEASURES a se:Evidence ;
     se:context "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a Chapter 12 section 2.3.1, printed pages 12-8 to 12-9." ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:evidence_type "DIRECT_SOURCE_PARAPHRASE" ;
     se:extraction_status "EXTRACTED_PENDING_REVIEW" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PENDING_REVIEW" ;
     se:limitations "The section names the measurements and their informal definitions only; formal measurement theory is out of anchor scope." ;
     se:method "Direct inspection of the official SWEBOK v4.0a PDF on 2026-11-07 at the verified page indices; original paraphrase." ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:result "The three named measurements and the failure-data-to-reliability-model chain were confirmed for the reliability measurement claim and the reliability concept." ;
     se:source_locator_ref se:LOC-07D-SWEBOK-KA12-QUALITY-MEASUREMENT ;
     se:statement "SWEBOK v4.0a KA12 section 2.3.1 states that software quality measurements support decision-making and names three widely used software quality measurements: error density (number of errors per unit size of documents or software), defect density (number of defects found divided by the size of the software) and failure rate (mean time to failure). It further states that reliability models are built from failure data collected during software testing or from software in service, and can therefore be used to estimate the probability of future failures and to assist in decisions about when to stop testing." ;
     se:synthetic "false"^^xsd:boolean .

