     se:source_locator_ref se:LOC-07D-SWEBOK-KA12-DEPENDABILITY ;
     se:statement "SWEBOK v4.0a KA12 section 1.4, in the context of safety-critical and software-intensive systems, names three complementary techniques for reducing failure risk — avoidance, detection and removal, and damage limitation — and states that these techniques impact software functional requirements, performance requirements and development processes. It adds that increasing risk implies increasing software quality assurance and more rigorous review techniques, and describes the assurance case as a reasoned, auditable artifact supporting the contention that claims are satisfied, containing claims about properties, arguments that logically link the evidence and assumptions to the claims, and a body of evidence and assumptions supporting the arguments." ;
     se:synthetic "false"^^xsd:boolean .

se:EVD-07D-SYNTHESIS-HOPE-BASED-OPS a se:Evidence ;
     se:context "Cross-source inference combining SWEBOK Guide v4.0a KA6 section 4.3 with CS2023 SE-Reliability Non-core topic 11; this is not a sentence that appears in either source." ;
