se:EVD-ARC-0005 a se:Evidence ;
     se:context "KA Core topic 5 with sub-topics 5a-5e and KA Core illustrative learning outcome 5 of the SE-Design unit." ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-06" ;
     se:evidence_type "DIRECT_SOURCE_PARAPHRASE" ;
     se:extraction_status "EXTRACTED_PENDING_REVIEW" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PENDING_REVIEW" ;
     se:limitations "Curriculum teaching guidance; not professional API-design consensus or a standard." ;
     se:method "Verbatim topic and learning-outcome text from the 2026-11-06 full-text extraction of the official Body of Knowledge PDF." ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:result "API contract documentation and error-reporting expectations are stated as KA Core curriculum content." ;
     se:source_locator_ref se:LOC-CS2023-SE-DESIGN-KU ;
     se:statement "CS2023 SE-Design covers API design principles in KA Core topic 5: consistency, where consistent APIs are easier to learn and less error-prone and consistency is both internal (between different portions of the API) and external (following common API patterns); composability; documenting contracts, where API operations should describe their effect on the system but not generally their implementation, including preconditions, postconditions and invariants; expandability; and error reporting, where errors should be clear, predictable and actionable, input that does not match the contract should produce an error, and errors that can be reliably managed without reporting should be managed. A KA Core illustrative learning outcome asks students to design an API for a single component of a large software system, including identifying and documenting each operation's invariants, contract and error conditions." ;
     se:synthetic "false"^^xsd:boolean .

