se:EVD-REQ-SWEBOK-CHANGE-SCOPE a se:Evidence ;
     se:context "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a Chapter 1 sections 6 (6.1-6.3) and 7 (7.1-7.4), printed pages 1-16 to 1-19." ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-06" ;
     se:evidence_type "DIRECT_SOURCE_PARAPHRASE" ;
     se:extraction_status "EXTRACTED_PENDING_REVIEW" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PENDING_REVIEW" ;
     se:limitations "The sections describe generally accepted activities; they do not assert that every project must instantiate all listed elements." ;
     se:method "Direct inspection of the official SWEBOK v4.0a PDF on 2026-11-06 at the verified page indices; original paraphrase." ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:result "The management-activities framing, change-control elements, scope-matching rule and the prioritization/tracing/stability considerations were confirmed." ;
     se:source_locator_ref se:LOC-SWEBOK-KA1-MANAGEMENT ;
     se:statement "SWEBOK v4.0a KA1 frames requirements management as maintaining the agreed requirements over time: requirements scrubbing, change control (request channel, optional impact analysis, an acceptance authority, notification and closure tracking, with plan-based and Agile life cycles handling it explicitly versus implicitly) and scope matching (keeping the requirements scope within cost, schedule and staffing constraints, quantitatively where possible). Its practical-considerations topics add that prioritization should weigh both the satisfaction a requirement creates and the dissatisfaction its absence causes, that tracing serves consistency accounting and change-impact analysis, and that identifying volatile requirements supports change-tolerant design." ;
     se:synthetic "false"^^xsd:boolean .

se:EVD-REQ-SWEBOK-ELICITATION a se:Evidence ;
     se:context "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a Chapter 1 section 2 (2.1 Requirements Sources; 2.2 Common Requirements Elicitation Techniques), printed pages 1-6 to 1-7." ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-06" ;
     se:evidence_type "DIRECT_SOURCE_PARAPHRASE" ;
     se:extraction_status "EXTRACTED_PENDING_REVIEW" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PENDING_REVIEW" ;
     se:limitations "The Guide's technique list is a survey of generally accepted techniques, not a comparative effectiveness ranking." ;
     se:method "Direct inspection of the official SWEBOK v4.0a PDF (SHA-256 0c9db4da0b2425c58cf778b99131eb31bb6c188e98b67163a549a1366d96e511) on 2026-11-06; text extracted at the verified page indices and paraphrased originally." ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:result "The elicitation activity's goal, source typology and technique families were confirmed for the professional-BOK scoped claim." ;
     se:source_locator_ref se:LOC-SWEBOK-KA1-ELICITATION ;
     se:statement "SWEBOK v4.0a KA1 presents requirements elicitation as an active activity whose goal is to surface candidate requirements and thereby minimize (though not eliminate) incompleteness: it names stakeholder classes (clients, customers, users, subject matter experts, operations and support staff, regulators and others) plus non-person sources (documentation, other systems, business context, computing environment), and lists technique families including interviews, facilitated workshops, questionnaires and surveys, exploratory prototyping, user story mapping, observation and apprenticing, noting that stakeholders may be tacit, unarticulate or uncooperative and that elicitation is not passive." ;
     se:synthetic "false"^^xsd:boolean .

se:EVD-REQ-SWEBOK-VALIDATION-METHODS a se:Evidence ;
     se:context "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a Chapter 1 section 5 (5.1-5.3), printed pages 1-15 to 1-16." ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-06" ;
     se:evidence_type "DIRECT_SOURCE_PARAPHRASE" ;
     se:extraction_status "EXTRACTED_PENDING_REVIEW" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PENDING_REVIEW" ;
     se:limitations "The section names the three methods without prescribing when each must be used." ;
     se:method "Direct inspection of the official SWEBOK v4.0a PDF on 2026-11-06 at the verified page indices; original paraphrase." ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:result "The validation definition and the three-method enumeration were confirmed for the professional-BOK scoped claim." ;
     se:source_locator_ref se:LOC-SWEBOK-KA1-VALIDATION ;
     se:statement "SWEBOK v4.0a KA1 defines requirements validation as gaining confidence that the requirements represent the stakeholders' true needs as currently understood, and names three methods that tend to be used: requirements reviews (preferably from multiple perspectives — stakeholders, specification experts and downstream designers/implementers), simulation or execution of the specification where the requirements are formally or model-based specified, and prototyping where direct simulation or execution is not possible." ;
     se:synthetic "false"^^xsd:boolean .

se:EVD-REQ-SYNTHESIS-QA-DEFERRED a se:Evidence ;
     se:context "Cross-topic inference combining KA Core topics 1 and 4 of the SE-Requirements unit; this is not a sentence that appears in CS2023." ;
