se:EVD-TVV-0010 a se:Evidence ;
     se:context "Secure-development practice PW.8 (test executable code) and its two tasks; executable code includes binaries, directly executed bytecode and source code." ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-06" ;
     se:evidence_type "DIRECT_SOURCE_PARAPHRASE" ;
     se:extraction_status "EXTRACTED_PENDING_REVIEW" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PENDING_REVIEW" ;
     se:limitations "Notional examples are explicitly neither required nor exhaustive.", "Recommendation-framework content: practice selection is governed by risk, cost, feasibility and applicability." ;
     se:method "Page-level inspection of the locally downloaded official NIST PDF (SHA-256 recorded in SEK-06C observation); verbatim task text anchored at printed page 15." ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:result "Notional implementation examples include choosing testing methods based on the stage of the software, incorporating tests for previously reported vulnerabilities into the project's test suite to ensure errors are not reintroduced, and using fuzz testing tools to find issues with input handling." ;
     se:source_locator_ref se:LOC-NIST-218-PW8 ;
     se:statement "NIST SSDF v1.1 task PW.8.1 directs determining whether executable code testing should be performed to find vulnerabilities not identified by previous reviews, analysis or testing and, if so, which types of testing should be used; task PW.8.2 directs scoping the testing, designing the tests, performing the testing and documenting the results, including recording and triaging all discovered issues and recommended remediations in the development team's workflow or issue tracking system." ;
     se:synthetic "false"^^xsd:boolean .

se:EVD-TVV-0011 a se:Evidence ;
     se:context "RV group structure spanning ongoing identification, risk-based disposition and root-cause learning." ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-06" ;
     se:evidence_type "DIRECT_SOURCE_PARAPHRASE" ;
     se:extraction_status "EXTRACTED_PENDING_REVIEW" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PENDING_REVIEW" ;
     se:limitations "Framework structure of SP 800-218 v1.1 only; not a universal vulnerability-management taxonomy.", "Practice order in the group does not imply implementation sequence." ;
     se:method "Page-level inspection of the locally downloaded official NIST PDF (SHA-256 recorded in SEK-06C observation); practices anchored at printed pages 16-18." ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_locator_ref se:LOC-NIST-218-RV ;
     se:statement "The Respond to Vulnerabilities (RV) group of NIST SSDF v1.1 comprises three practices: RV.1 identify and confirm vulnerabilities on an ongoing basis, with task RV.1.2 reviewing, analyzing and/or testing the software's code to identify or confirm previously undetected vulnerabilities and explicitly cross-referencing PW.7 and PW.8; RV.2 assess, prioritize and remediate vulnerabilities so that remediation occurs in accordance with risk, with task RV.2.1 analyzing each vulnerability to gather sufficient risk information to plan remediation or another risk response; and RV.3 analyze vulnerabilities to identify their root causes, with task RV.3.1 determining the root causes of each vulnerability." ;
     se:synthetic "false"^^xsd:boolean .

