se:EVD-TVV-0014 a se:Evidence ;
     se:context "Derived anti-pattern basis for se:ANT-TVV-COVERAGE-THEATER; synthesis of CS2023 SE-Validation topics 3, 6b and 8d with NIST PW.8.2 Example 3." ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-06" ;
     se:evidence_type "SYNTHESIS" ;
     se:extraction_status "EXTRACTED_PENDING_REVIEW" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PENDING_REVIEW" ;
     se:limitations "Synthesis inference, not a claim printed in any source; flagged for reviewer scrutiny." ;
     se:method "Author synthesis across the two admitted evidence families; no single source states the anti-pattern." ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_locator_ref se:LOC-CS2023-SE-VALIDATION-KU ;
     se:statement "Lane synthesis combining two admitted sources: CS2023 frames test coverage as three dimensions (test matrices, code coverage, environment coverage), lists distinct testing objectives including conformance to specification, and teaches an explicit tradeoff between test coverage and testing throughput/latency; NIST's notional regression-testing example targets specific previously reported vulnerabilities rather than aggregate coverage. On that combined basis, treating a code-coverage percentage as the whole of test coverage, or reading a passing test suite as proof of correctness or product validity, is unsupported by either source." ;
     se:synthetic "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
     se:uncertainty "Whether practitioners universally recognize this failure mode was not measured." .

