se:EVD-TVV-SWEBOK-FAULTS-ORACLES-LIMITS a se:Evidence ;
     se:context "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a Chapter 5 section 1 (1.1, 1.2.7, 1.2.8), printed pages 5-3 to 5-5." ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-06" ;
     se:evidence_type "DIRECT_SOURCE_PARAPHRASE" ;
     se:extraction_status "EXTRACTED_PENDING_REVIEW" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PENDING_REVIEW" ;
     se:limitations "The limitation statement is the Guide's reported testing-theory position; the Guide does not quantify attainable confidence." ;
     se:method "Direct inspection of the official SWEBOK v4.0a PDF (SHA-256 0c9db4da0b2425c58cf778b99131eb31bb6c188e98b67163a549a1366d96e511) on 2026-11-06; original paraphrase." ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:result "The fault/failure distinction, the oracle concept and the presence-not-absence limitation were confirmed for the professional-BOK scoped claim." ;
     se:source_locator_ref se:LOC-SWEBOK-KA5-FUNDAMENTALS ;
     se:statement "SWEBOK v4.0a KA5 distinguishes a fault (the cause of a malfunction) from a failure (the undesired effect observed in delivered service), noting that faults may never manifest as failures and that a failure's cause cannot always be unequivocally identified. It defines the oracle as any human or mechanical agent deciding whether the system under test behaved correctly, with inconclusive outcomes possible and oracle automation difficult and expensive. It also records testing theory's warning against ascribing unjustified confidence to successful tests: the established results are negative, and testing can show the presence of defects but not their absence, since complete testing is not feasible." ;
     se:synthetic "false"^^xsd:boolean .

se:EVD-TVV-SWEBOK-LEVELS-OBJECTIVES a se:Evidence ;
     se:context "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a Chapter 5 section 2 (2.1 with 2.1.1-2.1.4, 2.2), printed pages 5-6 to 5-7." ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-06" ;
     se:evidence_type "DIRECT_SOURCE_PARAPHRASE" ;
     se:extraction_status "EXTRACTED_PENDING_REVIEW" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PENDING_REVIEW" ;
     se:limitations "The stage list is target-based; objective-based taxonomies in the same chapter add further test types not covered by this locator." ;
     se:method "Direct inspection of the official SWEBOK v4.0a PDF on 2026-11-06; original paraphrase." ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:result "The four-stage target-based taxonomy with its no-process-implication caveat and the objective-stating guidance were confirmed." ;
     se:source_locator_ref se:LOC-SWEBOK-KA5-LEVELS-OBJECTIVES ;
     se:statement "SWEBOK v4.0a KA5 distinguishes four test stages by the target of the test — unit (separately testable elements in isolation), integration (interactions among elements, with incremental strategies such as top-down, bottom-up, mixed and big bang), system and acceptance — and states that these stages do not imply any development process and that none is assumed more important than the others. It adds that testing is conducted against specific objectives, and that stating objectives in precise, quantitative terms supports measurement and control of the test process." ;
     se:synthetic "false"^^xsd:boolean .

se:EVD-TVV-SWEBOK-TECHNIQUE-CLASSES a se:Evidence ;
     se:context "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a Chapter 5 section 3 (intro, 3.1, 3.2, 3.3 heading), printed pages 5-10 to 5-13." ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-06" ;
     se:evidence_type "DIRECT_SOURCE_PARAPHRASE" ;
     se:extraction_status "EXTRACTED_PENDING_REVIEW" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PENDING_REVIEW" ;
     se:limitations "The classification names the classes; technique-by-technique detail beyond the inspected pages is not covered by this locator." ;
     se:method "Direct inspection of the official SWEBOK v4.0a PDF on 2026-11-06; original paraphrase." ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:result "The black-box/white-box/experience-based classification and its overlap caveat were confirmed." ;
     se:source_locator_ref se:LOC-SWEBOK-KA5-TECHNIQUES ;
     se:statement "SWEBOK v4.0a KA5 classifies test techniques by the kind of information available about the system under test: specification-based (black-box) techniques generate test cases only from input/output behavior, while structure-based (white-box, also called glass-box or clear-box) techniques use information about how the system was designed or coded; experience-based techniques form a further class, and the Guide notes classification overlap and combination of techniques." ;
     se:synthetic "false"^^xsd:boolean .

se:GAP-07A-CS2023-CURRICULUM-SCOPE a se:CoverageGap ;
     se:coverage_status "OPEN" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:description "The registry-verified CS2023 Software Engineering knowledge-unit list (nine units: Teamwork; Tools and Environments; Product Requirements; Software Design; Software Construction; Software Verification and Validation; Refactoring and Code Evolution; Software Reliability; Formal Methods) contains no unit for engineering processes, lifecycle models or quality models, so this lane has no curriculum-side anchor for its scope and admits no CS2023-derived records." ;
     se:gap_kind "COVERAGE_GAP" ;
     se:impact "Curriculum-versus-professional-BOK comparison for process, lifecycle and quality-model scope is not possible from this lane; the lane's records rest on the professional-BOK source only." ;
     se:label "No CS2023 curriculum unit covers process, lifecycle or quality models" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PROPOSED" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:resolution_notes "If a curriculum comparator for this scope is needed, identify and register a curriculum source that actually covers it; do not stretch CS2023 units beyond their verified scope." ;
     se:severity "LOW" ;
     se:target_scope_ref se:VIEW-07A-SWEBOK-PROCESS-LIFECYCLE .

se:GAP-07A-FOUNDATIONS-BREADTH a se:CoverageGap ;
     se:coverage_status "OPEN" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:description "This lane inspected SWEBOK KA18 sections 1-3 (the engineering process; engineering design including wicked problems; abstraction and encapsulation including alternate abstractions) and read sections 4-5 (empirical methods, statistical analysis) without admitting them as locators; KA16 Computing Foundations and KA17 Mathematical Foundations were not inspected at all, so the foundations view carries only the engineering-foundations slice relevant to process, lifecycle and quality-model scope." ;
     se:gap_kind "SOURCE_GAP" ;
     se:impact "Systems-thinking and foundations records are bounded to what KA18's inspected sections state; computing and mathematical foundations for this scope stay uncovered." ;
     se:label "Foundations coverage limited to inspected KA18 sections" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PROPOSED" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:resolution_notes "Admit KA18 sections 4-5 evidence, and inspect KA16/KA17, if foundations depth becomes a lane requirement." ;
