se:LOC-07A-SWEBOK-KA10-ASSESSMENT a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 10 Software Engineering Process, section 3 Software Process Assessment and Improvement (3.1 Overview, 3.2 Goal Question Metric, 3.3 Framework-Based Methods, 3.4 Process Assessment and Improvement in Agile); PDF page indices 228-229; printed pages 10-9 to 10-10" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "PDCA paradigm as empirical-evidence basis for decisions; GQM (measurable goals, change, evaluate effect); framework-based methods with process reference and assessment models (CMM, CMMI, ISO/IEC 33000 series/SPICE); Agile retrospectives as a continuous learning loop." .

se:LOC-07A-SWEBOK-KA10-FUNDAMENTALS a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 10 Software Engineering Process, section 1 Software Engineering Process Fundamentals (1.1 Introduction, 1.2 Software Engineering Process Definition); PDF page indices 220-222; printed pages 10-1 to 10-3" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "Engineering-process framing (interrelated activities transforming inputs into outputs while consuming resources); process definitions with inputs, activities and outputs; no ideal process exists — processes must be selected, adapted and applied per project and organizational context; process management supported by empirical measurement." .

se:LOC-07A-SWEBOK-KA10-LIFECYCLE-DEFINITION a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 10 Software Engineering Process, section 2.1 Life Cycle Definition, Process Categories, and Terminology and section 2.2 Rationale for Life Cycles; PDF page indices 222-224; printed pages 10-3 to 10-4" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "Life cycle definition (evolution from conception through retirement); software system life cycle spanning ideation to retirement incl. production, operation, evolution, acquisition, supply; four process categories (technical; technical management; organizational project-enabling; agreement); interrelated life cycle processes." .

se:LOC-07A-SWEBOK-KA10-LIFECYCLE-MODELS a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 10 Software Engineering Process, section 2.3 The Concepts of Process Models and Life Cycle Models, section 2.4 Some Paradigms for Development Life Cycle Models and section 2.5 Development Life Cycle Models and Their Engineering Dimension; PDF page indices 224-226; printed pages 10-5 to 10-7" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "Life cycle created in conformance with a selected life cycle model (SLCM); named models waterfall, V-model, incremental, spiral, Agile; paradigms predictive, iterative, evolutionary, incremental, continuous; waterfall predictive and document-driven, spiral evolutionary and risk-driven; Agile open-to-change claims and named misconceptions about Agile." .

se:LOC-07A-SWEBOK-KA10-MANAGEMENT-ADAPTATION a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 10 Software Engineering Process, section 2.6 The Management of SLCPs, section 2.7 Software Engineering Process Management, section 2.8 Software Life Cycle Adaptation and section 2.9 Practical Considerations; PDF page indices 226-228; printed pages 10-7 to 10-9" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "Six general life cycle stages (concept, development, production, utilization, support, retirement) not presumed sequential; process management definition and levels; life cycle adaptation steps with documented decisions and rationale; estimations and measurements essential; large processes without deliverables increase uncertainty." .

se:LOC-07A-SWEBOK-KA11-ANALYSIS a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 11 Software Engineering Models and Methods, section 3 Analysis of Models (3.1 Analyzing for Completeness, 3.2 Consistency, 3.3 Correctness, 3.4 Traceability, 3.5 Interaction); PDF page indices 236-238; printed pages 11-5 to 11-7" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "Model analysis techniques: completeness, consistency, correctness (syntactic and semantic), traceability (work-product dependency mapping; improves work-product management and process quality; enables change-impact analysis) and interaction (incl. simulation)." .

se:LOC-07A-SWEBOK-KA11-MODELING a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 11 Software Engineering Models and Methods, Introduction and section 1 Modeling (1.1 Modeling Principles, 1.2 Properties and Expression of Models); PDF page indices 232-234; printed pages 11-1 to 11-3" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "Models and methods impose structure on software engineering (systematic, repeatable); scope from a single life cycle phase to the complete life cycle regardless of the type of life cycle process model; three modeling principles (model the essentials; provide perspective; enable effective communications); completeness, consistency, correctness as model properties; model as an aggregation of abstractions." .

se:LOC-07A-SWEBOK-KA12-DEPENDABILITY a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 12 Software Quality, section 1.4 Software Dependability and Integrity Levels including 1.4.1 Dependability and 1.4.2 Integrity Levels of Software; PDF page indices 249-250; printed pages 12-5 to 12-6" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "Dependability regrouping availability, reliability, maintainability and supportability, safety and security; integrity levels as a risk-management method based on project-unique characteristics; assurance cases as reasoned, auditable artifacts of claims, arguments and evidence." .

se:LOC-07A-SWEBOK-KA12-QUALITY-CONCEPTS a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 12 Software Quality, Introduction and section 1 Software Quality Fundamentals (including 1.1 Software Engineering Culture and Ethics, 1.2 Value and Costs of Quality); PDF page indices 245-248; printed pages 12-1 to 12-4" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "Quality term overload (product characteristics; product quality; process quality); surveyed definitions sharing a conformance-to-requirements premise; software quality requirements distinguished from software quality; error/defect/failure terminology; quality planned early and assessed at life cycle milestones; SQA adapted to different life cycles; CoSQ conformance and nonconformance categories." .

se:LOC-07A-SWEBOK-KA18-DESIGN-ABSTRACTION a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 18 Engineering Foundations, section 2 Engineering Design (including 2.2 Design as a Problem-Solving Activity) and section 3 Abstraction and Encapsulation (including 3.4 Alternate Abstractions); PDF page indices 367-369; printed pages 18-2 to 18-4" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "Design affects life cycle costs; software design guided by features and quality attributes; design problems as wicked problems (define by solving); many feasible solutions, best-meeting-needs-economically focus; abstraction levels and hierarchies; encapsulation; alternate abstractions complementary rather than hierarchical, synchronization difficult." .

se:LOC-07A-SWEBOK-KA18-ENG-PROCESS a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 18 Engineering Foundations, Introduction and section 1 The Engineering Process; PDF page indices 366-367; printed pages 18-1 to 18-2" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "IEEE engineering definition (systematic, disciplined, quantifiable approach); software engineering based on skills and knowledge common to all engineering disciplines; the engineering process necessarily iterative across six steps (understand the real problem via root cause analysis; define selection criteria; identify all technically feasible solutions; evaluate; select; monitor performance)." .

se:LOC-07B-CS2023-SDF-PRACTICES-KU a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "Body of Knowledge, Software Development Fundamentals (SDF), knowledge unit 'SDF-Practices: Software Development Practices' (CS Core topics 1-4 and CS Core Illustrative Learning Outcomes 1, 2 and 4); heading and topic text verified by full-text extraction of the official PDF on 2026-11-07; printed page not independently confirmed" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-CS2023 ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "CS Core topics: basic testing including test case design; use of a general-purpose IDE including its debugger; programming style that improves readability; specifying functionality of a module in a natural language. Outcomes: develop module tests with varied test-design strategies; explain limitations of testing; apply basic style guidelines (comments, indentation, proper naming) to aid readability." .

se:LOC-07B-CS2023-SE-CONSTRUCTION-KU a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "Body of Knowledge, Software Engineering (SE), knowledge unit 'SE-Construction: Software Construction' (CS Core topics 1-2, KA Core topics 3-7, Non-core topics 8-14, and KA Core Illustrative Learning Outcomes 3-5, 7-9); heading and topic text verified by full-text extraction of the official PDF on 2026-11-07; printed page not independently confirmed, unit falls inside the registry-verified SE section span (SE Overview PDF page indices 174-176)" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-CS2023 ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "CS Core: practical small-scale testing (unit testing; test-driven development with its psychological rationale) and documentation (interface documentation with contracts/pre-post conditions/invariants; implementation documentation focused on tricky and non-obvious code). KA Core: coding style (style guides, commenting, naming); best practices for coding (defensive, secure, exception handling for robustness); debugging; logging; use of libraries and frameworks. Non-core: larger-scale testing, work sequencing, security problems, autogenerated documentation, green-field vs existing code base, release management, DevOps." .

