     se:verified_content_summary "KA Core topic 3 names testing tools including static and dynamic analysis tools; Illustrative Learning Outcome 4 asks students to describe how available static and dynamic test tools can be integrated into the software development environment." .

se:LOC-07B-SWEBOK-KA4-CODING-QUALITY a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 4 Software Construction, section 3 Practical Considerations, subsections 3.3 Coding and 3.6 Construction Quality; PDF page indices 104-106; printed pages 4-7 to 4-9" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "Coding-activity considerations (understandable source code and naming/layout, control structures, anticipated and exceptional error handling, code-level security breach prevention, resource exclusion discipline, source organization, code documentation, code tuning) and the primary construction-quality techniques (unit/integration testing, test-first development, assertions and defensive programming, debugging, inspections, technical reviews, static analysis) with their code-adjacent focus." .

se:LOC-07B-SWEBOK-KA4-INTEGRATION a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 4 Software Construction, section 3.7 Integration; PDF page indices 106-107; printed pages 4-9 to 4-10" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "Integration as a key construction activity; planning concerns (sequence, hardware, scaffolding, pre-integration testing degree, interim-version test points); phased (big bang) vs incremental integration with the named advantage list for incremental (easier error location, improved progress monitoring, earlier product delivery, improved customer relations) and the stubs/drivers/mocks scaffolding requirement; continuous integration as widely adopted practice." .

se:LOC-07B-SWEBOK-KA4-INTRO-FUNDAMENTALS a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 4 Software Construction, Introduction and section 1 Software Construction Fundamentals, including 1.1 Minimizing Complexity, 1.2 Anticipating and Embracing Change, 1.3 Constructing for Verification, 1.4 Reusing Assets and 1.5 Applying Standards in Construction; PDF page indices 98-101; printed pages 4-1 to 4-4" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "KA definition (detailed creation and maintenance of software through coding, verification, unit testing, integration testing and debugging), KA linkage to Design/Testing/CM/Quality/Management/Computing Foundations, and the five fundamentals: minimizing complexity (working-memory rationale; cyclomatic complexity; simple readable code over clever code), anticipating change, constructing for verification (four named technique families), reusing assets and applying standards." .

