     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "API definition (exported signatures plus semantic statements), six API design goals with the outlasts-implementations rationale and OpenAPI/API-first practice; assertions as executable predicates compiled in at development and out later, design by contract (preconditions/postconditions per routine), defensive programming against invalid inputs; error/exception handling policies and fault tolerance strategies." .

se:LOC-07C-CS2023-SEC-ENGINEERING a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "Body of Knowledge, Security (SEC) knowledge area, knowledge unit 'SEC-Engineering: Security Analysis, Design, and Engineering' (CS Core topics 1, 3, 4; KA Core topics 5, 6, 9); heading and topic text verified by full-text extraction of the official PDF on 2026-11-07; printed page not independently confirmed" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-CS2023 ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "Security engineering goals of systems remaining dependable despite errors, accidents or malicious adversaries; problem and situational analysis for system security; tradeoff analysis over time, cost, risk tolerance, risk acceptance and return on investment; KA Core adds security requirements, controls, threat and vulnerability analysis, security testing and assessment, and attestation of software products." .

se:LOC-07C-CS2023-SEC-FOUNDATIONS a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "Body of Knowledge, Security (SEC) knowledge area, knowledge unit 'SEC-Foundations: Foundational Security' (CS Core topics 1, 5, 6); heading and topic text verified by full-text extraction of the official PDF on 2026-11-07; printed page not independently confirmed" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-CS2023 ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "Security mindset with crosscutting concepts including confidentiality, integrity, availability, risk assessment and adversarial thinking; protection principles such as least privilege, open design, fail-safe defaults, defense in depth and zero trust; optimization considerations between security, privacy, performance and other design goals." .

se:LOC-07C-NIST218-PO1 a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "NIST SP 800-218 v1.1 PDF page indices 13-14 (one-based 14-15); printed pages 5-6; Section 2, Table 1 practice PO.1 (Define Security Requirements for Software Development) and tasks PO.1.1-PO.1.3" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-NIST-SP-800-218-V1-1 ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "Security requirements known at all times so they inform the whole SDLC; internal sources (policies, business objectives, risk management strategy) and external sources (laws, regulations); risk-based architecture and design requirements; requirements communicated to third-party component suppliers including provenance and integrity verification expectations." .

se:LOC-07C-NIST218-PW1 a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "NIST SP 800-218 v1.1 PDF page index 19 (one-based 20); printed page 11; Section 2, Table 1 practice PW.1 (Design Software to Meet Security Requirements and Mitigate Security Risks) and tasks PW.1.1-PW.1.3" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-NIST-SP-800-218-V1-1 ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "Secure by design: evaluate security requirements and likely operational risks, mitigate in design and architecture, justify relaxations; risk modeling forms include threat modeling, attack modeling and attack surface mapping; track security requirements, risks and design decisions with recorded responses and re-evaluated exceptions." .

se:LOC-07C-NIST218-PW2 a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "NIST SP 800-218 v1.1 PDF page index 20 (one-based 21); printed page 12; Section 2, Table 1 practice PW.2 (Review the Software Design to Verify Compliance with Security Requirements and Risk Information) and task PW.2.1" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-NIST-SP-800-218-V1-1 ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "Design review by a qualified person not involved with the design and/or automated toolchain processes to confirm and enforce meeting all security requirements and satisfactorily addressing identified risks; findings recorded as artifacts." .

se:LOC-07C-SWEBOK-KA13-CONSTRUCTION-TESTING a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 13 Software Security, section 4 Security Engineering for Software Systems, subsections 4.4 Construction for Security and 4.5 Security Testing; PDF page indices 266-267 (one-based 267-268); printed pages 13-4 to 13-5" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "Coding security into software via recommended rules (smallest privileged modules; validated or documented assumptions; error-status checking); CERT top-10 practices including input validation, least privilege, default deny, defense in depth; security testing dual purpose (requirements met; no known vulnerabilities) via static analysis and authorized dynamic testing." .

se:LOC-07C-SWEBOK-KA13-FUNDAMENTALS a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 13 Software Security, section 1 Software Security Fundamentals, including 1.1 Software Security and 1.2 Information Security; PDF page index 263 (one-based 264); printed page 13-1" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "Design-security-in preferred over post-development patching; every life cycle stage considered; vulnerabilities also introduced via third-party components; security as a product quality characteristic; confidentiality, integrity, availability (plus authenticity, accountability, non-repudiation, reliability); engineers define and maintain security properties through the life cycle." .

se:LOC-07C-SWEBOK-KA13-SECURITY-DESIGN a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 13 Software Security, section 4 Security Engineering for Software Systems, subsections 4.2 Security Design and 4.3 Security Patterns; PDF page index 266 (one-based 267); printed page 13-4" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "Preventing unauthorized disclosure, creation, change, deletion or denial of access; tolerating violations by limiting damage, continuing service, failing and recovering securely; access control as fundamental; careful cryptographic algorithm and key management; threat modeling to specify mitigating security design; security pattern as recurring problem plus well-proven generic solution." .

se:LOC-07C-SWEBOK-KA13-SECURITY-REQUIREMENTS a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 13 Software Security, section 4 Security Engineering for Software Systems, subsection 4.1 Security Requirements; PDF page indices 265-266 (one-based 266-267); printed pages 13-3 to 13-4" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "Security requirements engineering as elicitation, specification and prioritization considering threats (misuse and abuse cases), threat actors and security risk assessments; lifecycle-model choice may affect activity order; product revision implies revisiting security requirements; traceability through development." .

se:LOC-07C-SWEBOK-KA13-VULNERABILITY-MANAGEMENT a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 13 Software Security, section 4 Security Engineering for Software Systems, subsection 4.6 Vulnerability Management, and section 5 Software Security Tools, subsection 5.1 Security Vulnerability Checking Tools; PDF page indices 267-268 (one-based 268-269); printed pages 13-5 to 13-6" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "CVE, CWE and CAPEC as shared vulnerability and weakness knowledge bases; CVSS for vulnerability severity; security maintenance with vulnerability disclosure processes; source and binary analysis tools aid detection but cannot find all vulnerabilities." .

se:LOC-07D-CS2023-SE-RELIABILITY-KU a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "Body of Knowledge, Software Engineering (SE), knowledge unit 'SE-Reliability: Software Reliability' (KA Core topics 1-6, Non-core topics 7-11, Illustrative Learning Outcomes 1-3); heading and topic text verified by full-text extraction of the official PDF on 2026-11-07; printed page not independently confirmed, page anchor per registry: SE section spans PDF page indices 174-176" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-CS2023 ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "KA Core topics: reliability concept (probability of failure or mean time between failures; faults as cause of failures); identifying reliability requirements for different kinds of software; failures caused by defects and minimum-defect goal (inject fewer, remove more); software reliability vs system reliability and failure behavior; defect injection and removal cycle; error budget vs error-free approaches. Non-core topics: reliability models; fault tolerance techniques and models with contextual differences; reliability engineering practices; dependent and independent failure domains; measurement-based analysis (telemetry, monitoring and alerting, dashboards, release qualification metrics)." .

se:LOC-07D-SWEBOK-KA12-DEPENDABILITY a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 12 Software Quality, section 1.4 Software Dependability and Integrity Levels (including 1.4.1 Dependability and 1.4.2 Integrity Levels of Software); PDF page indices 249-250; printed pages 12-5 to 12-6" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "Safety-critical context; three complementary techniques for reducing failure risk — avoidance, detection and removal, and damage limitation — impacting functional requirements, performance requirements and development processes; increasing risk implies more rigorous SQA/review; assurance case as claims, arguments and supporting evidence/assumptions; integrity levels as risk management." .

se:LOC-07D-SWEBOK-KA12-QUALITY-MEASUREMENT a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 12 Software Quality, section 2.3.1 Software Quality Measurement; PDF page indices 252-253; printed pages 12-8 to 12-9" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "Quality measurements support decision-making; three widely used measurements: error density, defect density and failure rate (mean time to failure); reliability models built from failure data collected during testing or in service estimate probability of future failures and assist decisions about when to stop testing." .

se:LOC-07D-SWEBOK-KA6-AVAILABILITY-SLA a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 6 Software Engineering Operations, section 2.3 Software Availability, Continuity, and Service Levels; PDF page index 157; printed page 6-8" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "Availability and continuity managed against customer commitments; defined as nonfunctional requirements early; availability measured and recorded, unplanned nonavailability investigated; service reports give indicators against service-level targets; service-level management monitors agreed service level including workload, performance and availability trends; SLAs clarify operations obligations." .

se:LOC-07D-SWEBOK-KA6-CAPACITY a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 6 Software Engineering Operations, section 2.4 Software Capacity Management; PDF page index 157; printed page 6-8" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "Capacity at all times for current and future agreed demand; business predictions and workload estimates translated into documented requirements; predictable reaction to workload variation; component and resource-utilization data captured and analyzed; capacity plan (at least annually) with actual performance, expected requirements and costed options against SLA targets." .

se:LOC-07D-SWEBOK-KA6-DR-FAILOVER a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 6 Software Engineering Operations, section 2.5 Software Backup, Disaster Recovery, and Failover; PDF page indices 157-158; printed pages 6-8 to 6-9" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "Backups plus restoration equipment/staff quickly available after major failure; recovery need shapes backup method, restore-point frequency, storage and retention; preparedness and regular testing of backup, disaster recovery and failover rehearsed as production changes; failure is inevitable; automated failover daemons reduce recovery time drastically; applications should include failure-handling logic planned during development." .

se:LOC-07D-SWEBOK-KA6-MONITOR a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 6 Software Engineering Operations, section 4.3 Monitor, Measure, Track, and Review; PDF page index 160; printed page 6-11" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "Operations monitor capacity, continuity and availability; hope should not be a strategy; engineers should be informed about system quality and operational health with evidence — real-time KPIs including production monitoring and product telemetry, actionable V&V results before and after release, end-user activity and resource use, impact analysis results, operational dependencies, unapproved configuration changes, and security and resilience performance capability." .

se:LOC-07D-SWEBOK-KA6-PERF-REL-LB a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 6 Software Engineering Operations, section 1.6 Performance, Reliability and Load Balancing; PDF page index 155; printed page 6-6" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "Operations engineers plan performance, reliability and load balancing early in projects to meet project requirements; trend toward infrastructure/operations services that adjust dynamically to demand; DevOps lets operations anticipate needs early and expose infrastructure services for developers to use and test during development." .

se:LOC-07E-CS2023-SE-TOOLS-KU a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "Body of Knowledge, Software Engineering (SE), knowledge unit 'SE-Tools: Tools and Environments' (CS Core topic 1 with subtopics 1a-1c; KA Core topics 2-7 including 4a-4c; illustrative learning outcomes 4-6); heading and topic text verified by full-text extraction of the official PDF on 2026-11-07; page anchor per registry: SE-Tools unit at PDF page index 178 (one-based PDF page 179); printed page not independently confirmed" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-CS2023 ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "Build/CI/delivery-relevant curriculum topics: configuration in version control and reproducible builds/configuration; branching strategies (development vs release branches, trunk-based development); merging/rebasing; release management; software process automation (fast, hermetic, reproducible builds; CI as automated preliminary validation of head/trunk; dependency management, package management, SemVer); learning outcomes on CI as ground truth for shared code state." .

se:LOC-07E-SWEBOK-KA6-DEPLOY-RELEASE a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 6 Software Engineering Operations, section 3 Software Engineering Operations Delivery, subsection 3.2 Deployment/Release Engineering; PDF page index 159; printed page 6-10" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "Deployment (installing a specified version into an environment) vs release (making features available to customers or a segment); manual dev-to-ops hand-off characterized as inefficient; DevOps automation of deployment steps; environment-based vs application-based release strategies; canary release testing; automated rollback; release as a business decision." .

se:LOC-07E-SWEBOK-KA6-ENVIRONMENTS a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 6 Software Engineering Operations, section 2 Software Engineering Operations Planning, subsection 2.2 Development and Operational Environments; PDF page indices 156-157; printed pages 6-7 to 6-8" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "Development, testing/QA, preproduction and production environments must be coherent and synchronized with production; DevOps recommends automated environment creation built from a single code repository (single source of truth), leading to infrastructure as code." .

se:LOC-07E-SWEBOK-KA6-RELEASE-PLANNING a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 6 Software Engineering Operations, section 2 Software Engineering Operations Planning, subsection 2.1.1 Operations Plan (release and version planning tasks at the individual request level); PDF page index 156; printed page 6-7" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "Release/version planning tasks for validated individual requests: identify target availability dates, agree on the content of subsequent releases or versions, identify potential conflicts and develop alternatives, assess the risk of a given release and develop a rollback and data migration plan, inform all stakeholders." .

se:LOC-07E-SWEBOK-KA6-ROLLBACK a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 6 Software Engineering Operations, section 3 Software Engineering Operations Delivery, subsection 3.3 Rollback and Data Migration; PDF page indices 159-160; printed pages 6-10 to 6-11" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "Rollback and data migration return software and its database to a working state; a planned and rehearsed rollback precedes production deployment; DevOps automates the process and automated surveillance can trigger it; both release strategy categories can support rollback." .

se:LOC-07E-SWEBOK-KA8-BUILDING a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 8 Software Configuration Management, section 6 Software Release Management and Delivery (section introduction) and subsection 6.1 Software Building; PDF page index 196; printed page 8-13" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "Software building constructs the correct versions of SCIs with the appropriate configuration data into a package; SCM must usually reproduce previous releases and keep supporting tools and build instructions under control for exact rebuilds; the SBOM listing build artifacts is an important CM output; in CI, building is triggered automatically on commit and its artifacts are deployed through the release management process." .

se:LOC-07E-SWEBOK-KA8-LIBRARIES a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 8 Software Configuration Management, section 2 Software Configuration Identification, subsections 2.5 Relationships Scheme Definition (incl. the SBOM) and 2.6 Software Libraries; PDF page indices 191-192; printed pages 8-8 to 8-9" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "SBOM as a formal record of the details and supply-chain relationships of the components used in building software; software libraries as controlled collections whose binary objects carry cryptographic hashes for the physical configuration audit; the definitive media library holds the release baselines deployable to test, stage and production, and release management depends on these libraries." .

se:LOC-07E-SWEBOK-KA8-PLANNING a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 8 Software Configuration Management, section 1 Management of the SCM Process, subsections 1.3 Planning for SCM (incl. its branching/merging and continuous-integration paragraph) and 1.4 SCM Plan; PDF page indices 186-188; printed pages 8-3 to 8-5" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "Branching and merging strategies should be carefully planned and communicated because they affect many SCM activities; many development approaches use continuous integration characterized by frequent build-test-deploy cycles, requiring SCM planning accordingly; SCMP subordinate procedures define which branching strategies are used, how frequently builds occur and how often automated tests run." .

se:LOC-07E-SWEBOK-KA8-RELEASE-MGMT a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 8 Software Configuration Management, section 6 Software Release Management and Delivery, subsection 6.2 Software Release Management; PDF page indices 196-197; printed pages 8-13 to 8-14" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "Release as distributing software and related artifacts outside the development activity; release management as identification, packaging and delivery of product elements; the when-to-release decision informed by problem severity and prior-release fault densities; VDD, release notes, installation/upgrade instructions, distribution tracking and digital-signature integrity; the continuous-delivery pipeline." .

se:LOC-07F-CS2023-REFACTORING-KU a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "Body of Knowledge, Software Engineering (SE), knowledge unit 'SE-Refactoring: Refactoring and Code Evolution' (KA Core topics 1-4, Non-core topic 5); heading and topic text verified by full-text extraction of the official PDF on 2026-11-07; printed page not independently confirmed, page anchor per registry: SE section content spans PDF pages 174-177 (registry-recorded)" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-CS2023 ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "KA Core topics: Hyrum's Law/Law of Implicit Interfaces; backward compatibility (relationship property; provider+consumer evaluation); refactoring (standard patterns, IDE tools, static-analysis application, value as technical-debt remedy); versioning (SemVer, trunk-based development). Non-core: large-scale refactoring (coexisting old/new APIs, minimized behavior change, unseen consumers)." .

se:LOC-07F-SWEBOK-KA7-CATEGORIES a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
