se:LOC-07G-SWEBOK-KA15-DECISION-PROCESS a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 15 Software Engineering Economics, section 2 The Engineering Decision-Making Process (2.1 Process Overview through 2.7 Monitor the Performance of the Selected Alternative); PDF page indices 291-293; printed pages 15-5 to 15-7" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "Six-step decision process (understand the real problem; identify all reasonable technically feasible solutions; define selection criteria; evaluate each alternative on the same basis and planning horizon; select; monitor performance); effort scaled to consequences of a wrong decision; decision-making-under-risk vs. under-uncertainty technique families; closing the loop on estimates against actual outcomes." .

se:LOC-07G-SWEBOK-KA15-ESTIMATION a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 15 Software Engineering Economics, section 8 Estimation (8.1 Expert Judgment, 8.2 Analogy, 8.3 Decomposition, 8.4 Parametric, 8.5 Multiple Estimates); PDF page indices 299-302; printed pages 15-13 to 15-16" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "Estimates as inherently uncertain analytical predictions made to support decisions; Code of Ethics clause 3.09 quoted (realistic quantitative estimates with uncertainty assessment); five general techniques with availability/accuracy trade-offs; multiple-estimate convergence/divergence reading." .

se:LOC-07G-SWEBOK-KA15-INTRO a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 15 Software Engineering Economics, Introduction (value-based software engineering; engineering economics question; software technical decisions across the product life cycle; unquantifiable criteria) and Breakdown of Topics incl. Figure 15.1; PDF page indices 287-288; printed pages 15-1 to 15-2" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "Software engineering must be value-based; economics framed as the science of choice; technical decisions (e.g., reuse a preexisting library vs. develop own) carry business implications; economic perspective applies from pre-project to end-of-life decisions at all levels of technical detail; unquantifiable criteria must also be considered." .

se:LOC-07G-SWEBOK-KA9-ESTIMATION a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 9 Software Engineering Management, section 2 Software Project Planning, subsection 2.3 Effort, Schedule, and Cost Estimation; PDF page indices 208-209; printed pages 9-8 to 9-9" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "Estimating software costs characterized as error-prone (human elements and dynamic factors); advice to use multiple estimation approaches and reconcile differences; calibrated models plus bottom-up estimates; iterative negotiation among stakeholders; predictive vs. adaptive scheduling differences." .

se:LOC-07G-SWEBOK-KA9-INTRO a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "ACTIVE" ;
     se:locator "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 9 Software Engineering Management, Introduction (software engineering management definition; measurement-informed management discussion; working definitions of management and measurement; seven-topic activity-based breakdown incl. Figure 9.1); PDF page indices 201-206; printed pages 9-1 to 9-6" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "SEM defined as planning, estimating, measuring, controlling, coordinating, leading and managing risk for a software project; management without measurement suggests a lack of discipline and measurement without management a lack of purpose or context; seven activity-based topics listed." .

se:LOC-07G-SWEBOK-KA9-MEASUREMENT a se:SourceLocator ;
     se:accessed_on "2026-11-07" ;
