     se:locator "SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 9 Software Engineering Management, section 6 Software Engineering Measurement (6.1 Establish and Sustain Measurement Commitment, 6.2 Plan the Measurement Process, 6.3 Perform the Measurement Process, 6.4 Evaluate Measurement); PDF page indices 214-216; printed pages 9-14 to 9-16" ;
     se:locator_type "SECTION" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:source_ref se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A ;
     se:verification_state "LOCATOR_VERIFIED" ;
     se:verified_content_summary "Measurement program presented as following ISO/IEC/IEEE 15939: objectives-driven measurement requirements and committed resources; information needs identified from the organizational unit's goals/constraints/risks/problems; measures selected against criteria such as collection cost and process disruption; procedures integrated into measured processes; evaluation against criteria with lessons learned." .

se:LOC-07G-SWEBOK-KA9-RISK-QUALITY a se:SourceLocator ;
