se:NODE-07A-KA10-SWE-PROCESS a se:TaxonomyNode ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:definition "The SWEBOK Guide v4.0a knowledge area covering software engineering process fundamentals, life cycles and life cycle models, process management and life cycle adaptation, and software process assessment and improvement; the Guide positions it as closely related to several other KAs, naming Software Engineering Management, Software Engineering Models and Methods, Software Quality, Software Architecture and Software Testing." ;
     se:evidence_refs se:EVD-07A-KA10-PROCESS-DEFINITION ;
     se:label "SWEBOK KA10 Software Engineering Process" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PROPOSED" ;
     se:node_kind "KNOWLEDGE_AREA" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:view_ref se:VIEW-07A-SWEBOK-PROCESS-LIFECYCLE .

se:NODE-07A-KA12-SOFTWARE-QUALITY a se:TaxonomyNode ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:definition "The SWEBOK Guide v4.0a knowledge area covering software quality fundamentals (quality concepts, engineering culture and ethics, value and costs of quality, standards/models/certifications, dependability and integrity levels), the software quality management and assurance processes, and quality tools; represented in this lane only at the model level." ;
     se:evidence_refs se:EVD-07A-KA12-QUALITY-OVERLOAD ;
     se:label "SWEBOK KA12 Software Quality" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PROPOSED" ;
     se:node_kind "KNOWLEDGE_AREA" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:view_ref se:VIEW-07A-SWEBOK-QUALITY-MODELS .

se:NODE-07A-KA18-FOUNDATIONS a se:TaxonomyNode ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:definition "The SWEBOK Guide v4.0a foundation knowledge area covering the engineering process, engineering design, abstraction and encapsulation, empirical methods and experimental techniques, and statistical analysis, presented as pertinent to all engineering disciplines including software engineering." ;
     se:evidence_refs se:EVD-07A-KA18-ENG-PROCESS ;
     se:label "SWEBOK KA18 Engineering Foundations" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PROPOSED" ;
     se:node_kind "KNOWLEDGE_AREA" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:view_ref se:VIEW-07A-SWEBOK-ENGINEERING-FOUNDATIONS .

se:NODE-07A-LIFECYCLE-MODELS a se:TaxonomyNode ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:definition "The KA10 topic grouping development life cycle models (waterfall, V-model, incremental, spiral and Agile, among others) and their paradigms (predictive, iterative, evolutionary, incremental, continuous), in which a specific life cycle is created in conformance with a selected life cycle model." ;
     se:evidence_refs se:EVD-07A-KA10-LIFECYCLE-MODELS ;
     se:label "Development life cycle models and paradigms (SWEBOK KA10 sections 2.3-2.5)" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PROPOSED" ;
     se:node_kind "SUBDOMAIN" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:view_ref se:VIEW-07A-SWEBOK-PROCESS-LIFECYCLE .

se:NODE-07A-PROCESS-ASSESSMENT a se:TaxonomyNode ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:definition "The KA10 topic grouping software process assessment and improvement approaches: the Shewhart-Deming PDCA paradigm, the Goal Question Metric approach, framework-based methods (CMM, CMMI and the ISO/IEC 33000 series) and Agile-life-cycle retrospectives." ;
     se:evidence_refs se:EVD-07A-KA10-ASSESSMENT ;
     se:label "Software process assessment and improvement (SWEBOK KA10 section 3)" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PROPOSED" ;
     se:node_kind "PRACTICE_GROUP" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:view_ref se:VIEW-07A-SWEBOK-PROCESS-LIFECYCLE .

se:NODE-07A-QUALITY-REQUIREMENTS a se:TaxonomyNode ;
     se:CROSS_CUTS se:NODE-07A-KA10-SWE-PROCESS ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:definition "The KA12 category of software quality requirements: attributes of, or constraints on, functional requirements — commonly shorthand'd as \"the -ilities\" — distinguished from software quality itself and expected to be defined by the software requirements together with the measurement methods and acceptance criteria for assessing quality." ;
     se:evidence_refs se:EVD-07A-KA12-QUALITY-OVERLOAD ;
     se:label "Software quality requirements (the -ilities)" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PROPOSED" ;
     se:node_kind "QUALITY_ATTRIBUTE" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:view_ref se:VIEW-07A-SWEBOK-QUALITY-MODELS .

se:NODE-07B-CS2023-SDF-PRACTICES a se:TaxonomyNode ;
     se:SUPPORTED_BY se:EVD-07B-CS2023-SDF-PRACTICES ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:definition "The Software Development Practices knowledge unit of the CS2023 Software Development Fundamentals area, prescribing basic testing with test case design, use of a general-purpose IDE with its debugger, programming style that improves readability, and specifying module functionality in natural language at CS Core level." ;
     se:evidence_refs se:EVD-07B-CS2023-SDF-PRACTICES ;
     se:label "CS2023 SDF-Practices: Software Development Practices" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PROPOSED" ;
     se:node_kind "KNOWLEDGE_UNIT" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:view_ref se:VIEW-07B-CS2023-SDF .

se:NODE-07B-CS2023-SE-CONSTRUCTION a se:TaxonomyNode ;
     se:RELATED_TO se:SUB-07B-SOFTWARE-CONSTRUCTION ;
     se:SUPPORTED_BY se:EVD-07B-CS2023-CORE-HOURS ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:definition "The Software Construction knowledge unit of the CS2023 Software Engineering area: practical small-scale testing and documentation as CS Core, with coding style, coding best practices, debugging, logging and use of external libraries and frameworks as KA Core, and larger-scale testing, work sequencing, security problems, autogenerated documentation, development context and release/DevOps topics as Non-core." ;
     se:evidence_refs se:EVD-07B-CS2023-CORE-HOURS ;
     se:label "CS2023 SE-Construction: Software Construction" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PROPOSED" ;
     se:node_kind "KNOWLEDGE_UNIT" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:view_ref se:VIEW-CS2023-SE .

se:NODE-07C-SECURE-DESIGN a se:TaxonomyNode ;
     se:PART_OF se:NODE-07C-SECURITY-LIFECYCLE ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:definition "Security design concerns — preventing unauthorized disclosure, creation, change, deletion or denial of access, tolerating attacks by limiting damage and failing and recovering securely, access control and cryptographic material handling, threat modeling for mitigation, and security patterns — per SWEBOK KA13 4.2-4.3 and SSDF practice PW.1." ;
     se:evidence_refs se:EVD-07C-NIST-PW1-SECURE-BY-DESIGN, se:EVD-07C-SWEBOK-SECURITY-DESIGN ;
     se:label "Secure design and architecture" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PROPOSED" ;
     se:node_kind "CONCERN" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:view_ref se:VIEW-07C-SECURITY-ENGINEERING .

se:NODE-07C-SECURE-IMPLEMENTATION a se:TaxonomyNode ;
     se:PART_OF se:NODE-07C-SECURITY-LIFECYCLE ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:definition "Construction-time security practices: coding security into software through recommended rules (least-privilege modules, validated assumptions, error-status checking) and protection principles (input validation, default deny, defense in depth), per SWEBOK KA13 4.4 and the CS2023 SEC-Foundations protection-principles topic." ;
     se:evidence_refs se:EVD-07C-CS2023-SEC-FOUNDATIONS, se:EVD-07C-SWEBOK-CONSTRUCTION-RULES ;
     se:label "Secure implementation practices" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PROPOSED" ;
     se:node_kind "PRACTICE_GROUP" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:view_ref se:VIEW-07C-SECURITY-ENGINEERING .

se:NODE-07C-SECURITY-LIFECYCLE a se:TaxonomyNode ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:definition "The lane's organizing node: security requirements, secure design, secure implementation and security verification concerns that span development life cycle stages rather than belonging to a single phase, grounded in the design-security-in framing of SWEBOK KA13 section 1 and the SSDF secure-by-design practice PW.1." ;
     se:evidence_refs se:EVD-07C-NIST-PW1-SECURE-BY-DESIGN, se:EVD-07C-SWEBOK-SECURITY-BY-DESIGN ;
     se:label "Security as a lifecycle-cross-cutting concern" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PROPOSED" ;
     se:node_kind "CONCERN" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:view_ref se:VIEW-07C-SECURITY-ENGINEERING .

se:NODE-07C-SECURITY-REQUIREMENTS a se:TaxonomyNode ;
     se:PART_OF se:NODE-07C-SECURITY-LIFECYCLE ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:definition "Security requirements work — elicitation, specification, prioritization and maintenance over time — informed by threats (misuse and abuse cases), threat actors and security risk assessments, kept traceable through development, per SWEBOK KA13 4.1 and SSDF practice PO.1." ;
     se:evidence_refs se:EVD-07C-NIST-PO1-REQUIREMENTS, se:EVD-07C-SWEBOK-SECURITY-REQUIREMENTS ;
     se:label "Threat- and risk-informed security requirements" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PROPOSED" ;
     se:node_kind "CONCERN" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:view_ref se:VIEW-07C-SECURITY-ENGINEERING .

se:NODE-07C-SECURITY-VERIFICATION a se:TaxonomyNode ;
     se:DEPENDS_ON se:NODE-07C-SECURITY-REQUIREMENTS ;
     se:PART_OF se:NODE-07C-SECURITY-LIFECYCLE ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:definition "Verifying that implemented software meets its security requirements and contains none of the known vulnerabilities (static analysis and authorized dynamic testing), handling residual vulnerabilities (categorized weakness knowledge bases, severity scoring, disclosure processes), and the tool-limit boundary that checking tools cannot find all vulnerabilities — per SWEBOK KA13 4.5-4.6 and 5.1." ;
     se:evidence_refs se:EVD-07C-SWEBOK-SECURITY-TESTING, se:EVD-07C-SWEBOK-VULNERABILITY-DATABASES ;
     se:label "Security verification, vulnerability handling and assurance" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PROPOSED" ;
     se:node_kind "CONCERN" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:view_ref se:VIEW-07C-SECURITY-ENGINEERING .

se:NODE-07D-CS2023-SE-RELIABILITY a se:TaxonomyNode ;
     se:RELATED_TO se:NODE-07D-RELIABILITY-RESILIENCE ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:definition "The Software Reliability knowledge unit of the CS2023 Software Engineering area: a KA Core unit (2 KA Core hours, no CS Core hours) whose core topics cover the reliability concept, reliability requirements, defects and reliability, software versus system reliability, the defect injection and removal cycle, and the error-budget versus error-free comparison, with non-core topics on reliability models, fault tolerance, reliability engineering practices, failure domains and measurement-based analysis." ;
     se:evidence_refs se:EVD-07D-CS2023-RELIABILITY-CORE-HOURS, se:EVD-07D-CS2023-SE-RELIABILITY-KU ;
     se:label "CS2023 SE-Reliability: Software Reliability" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PROPOSED" ;
     se:node_kind "KNOWLEDGE_UNIT" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:view_ref se:VIEW-CS2023-SE .

se:NODE-07D-OBSERVABILITY-FEEDBACK a se:TaxonomyNode ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:definition "The operational concern of obtaining evidence about system quality and operational health — telemetry, monitoring and alerting, dashboards, reliability measurement and key performance indicators — so that operational decisions rest on observed data rather than assumption." ;
     se:evidence_refs se:EVD-07D-CS2023-MEASUREMENT-TELEMETRY, se:EVD-07D-SWEBOK-MONITOR-EVIDENCE ;
     se:label "Measurement and telemetry as the operational feedback mechanism" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PROPOSED" ;
     se:node_kind "CONCERN" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:view_ref se:VIEW-07D-RELIABILITY-PERFORMANCE .

se:NODE-07D-PERFORMANCE-CAPACITY a se:TaxonomyNode ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:definition "The operational concern cluster covering capacity and performance engineering: planning performance and load handling early, translating workload forecasts into capacity requirements, and managing resource utilization against agreed demand." ;
     se:evidence_refs se:EVD-07D-SWEBOK-CAPACITY-MGMT, se:EVD-07D-SWEBOK-PERF-RELIABILITY-EARLY ;
     se:label "Performance, capacity and resource efficiency" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PROPOSED" ;
     se:node_kind "QUALITY_ATTRIBUTE" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:view_ref se:VIEW-07D-RELIABILITY-PERFORMANCE .

se:NODE-07D-RELIABILITY-RESILIENCE a se:TaxonomyNode ;
     se:CROSS_CUTS se:NODE-07D-PERFORMANCE-CAPACITY ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:definition "The operational concern cluster covering failure behavior of software in service: reliability as a measured property, availability against service commitments, fault tolerance and failure-handling mechanisms, and resilience through recovery preparedness." ;
     se:evidence_refs se:EVD-07D-CS2023-RELIABILITY-CONCEPT, se:EVD-07D-SWEBOK-AVAILABILITY-SLA ;
     se:label "Reliability, availability, fault tolerance and resilience" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PROPOSED" ;
     se:node_kind "QUALITY_ATTRIBUTE" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:view_ref se:VIEW-07D-RELIABILITY-PERFORMANCE .

se:NODE-07E-SE-TOOLS-KU a se:TaxonomyNode ;
     se:CROSS_CUTS se:NODE-07E-SWEBOK-KA6-OPERATIONS, se:NODE-07E-SWEBOK-KA8-SCM ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:definition "The Tools and Environments knowledge unit of the CS2023 Software Engineering area; the build/CI/delivery-relevant topics this lane relies on are CS Core topic 1 (software configuration management and version control, including configuration in version control, reproducible builds/configuration, branching strategies and merging/rebasing) and KA Core topics 2 and 4 (release management; software process automation: build systems, continuous integration, dependency management)." ;
     se:evidence_refs se:EVD-07E-CS2023-TOOLS-KU ;
