se:NODE-07F-CHANGE-IMPACT-AND-CONTROL a se:TaxonomyNode ;
     se:SUPPORTED_BY se:EVD-07F-SWEBOK-IMPACT-ANALYSIS ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:definition "The concern of assessing the detailed effects proposed changes have on existing software (SWEBOK KA7 2.1.3 impact analysis) and of routing change requests through a formal evaluate-and-approve control process (SWEBOK KA8 3.1 software change request process, configuration control board), which KA7 locates after a change request enters the SCM process." ;
     se:evidence_refs se:EVD-07F-SWEBOK-IMPACT-ANALYSIS, se:EVD-07F-SWEBOK-KA8-SCR-PROCESS ;
     se:label "Change impact and change control" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PROPOSED" ;
     se:node_kind "CONCERN" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:view_ref se:VIEW-07F-MAINTENANCE-EVOLUTION .

se:NODE-07F-CS2023-SE-REFACTORING a se:TaxonomyNode ;
     se:RELATED_TO se:NODE-07F-REFACTORING-AND-TECH-DEBT ;
     se:SUPPORTED_BY se:EVD-07F-CS2023-REFACTORING-KU ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:definition "The Refactoring and Code Evolution knowledge unit of the CS2023 Software Engineering area, whose KA Core topics are Hyrum's Law (the Law of Implicit Interfaces), backward compatibility as a relationship property, refactoring (standard patterns, IDE tooling, static analysis, value as a technical-debt remedy) and versioning (Semantic Versioning, trunk-based development), with large-scale refactoring as a Non-core topic." ;
     se:evidence_refs se:EVD-07F-CS2023-REFACTORING-KU ;
     se:label "CS2023 SE-Refactoring: Refactoring and Code Evolution" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PROPOSED" ;
     se:node_kind "KNOWLEDGE_UNIT" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:view_ref se:VIEW-CS2023-SE .

se:NODE-07F-REFACTORING-AND-TECH-DEBT a se:TaxonomyNode ;
     se:SUPPORTED_BY se:EVD-07F-SWEBOK-REFACTORING ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:definition "The techniques SWEBOK KA7 sections 4.2/4.3 describe for evolving existing software: reengineering to reconstitute software in a new form (often to replace aging legacy software), refactoring to reorganize a program without changing behavior in order to improve internal structure and maintainability and reduce technical debt, passive reverse engineering to recover higher-abstraction representations, and the measurement of debt with size, complexity, flaw and practice-violation indicators (2.3.1)." ;
     se:evidence_refs se:EVD-07F-SWEBOK-REFACTORING, se:EVD-07F-SWEBOK-TECH-DEBT-COST ;
     se:label "Refactoring, reengineering and technical debt management" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PROPOSED" ;
     se:node_kind "KNOWLEDGE_UNIT" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:view_ref se:VIEW-07F-MAINTENANCE-EVOLUTION .

se:NODE-07F-SOFTWARE-MAINTENANCE a se:TaxonomyNode ;
     se:SUPPORTED_BY se:EVD-07F-SWEBOK-MAINT-DEFINITION ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:definition "The activity SWEBOK v4.0a KA7 defines as the totality of activities required to provide cost-effective support for software in operation, spanning pre-delivery preparation (planning for post-delivery operations, maintainability and logistics) and post-delivery activities (surveillance, modification, training, help-desk operation), with the reported ISO/IEC/IEEE 14764 objective of modifying existing software while preserving its integrity." ;
     se:evidence_refs se:EVD-07F-SWEBOK-MAINT-DEFINITION ;
     se:label "Software maintenance (post-delivery support of operational software)" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PROPOSED" ;
     se:node_kind "KNOWLEDGE_AREA" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:view_ref se:VIEW-07F-MAINTENANCE-EVOLUTION .

se:NODE-07G-CS2023-SE-TEAMWORK a se:TaxonomyNode ;
     se:CROSS_CUTS se:NODE-07G-SEM-PROJECT-PLANNING ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:definition "The Teamwork knowledge unit of the CS2023 Software Engineering area: CS Core topics on communication, conflict, cooperative programming, roles and responsibilities, team processes (responsibilities for tasks, effort estimation, meeting structure, work schedule) and diversity, with KA Core topics on interfacing with stakeholders as a team and on risks associated with physical, distributed, hybrid and virtual teams." ;
     se:evidence_refs se:EVD-07G-CS2023-TEAMWORK-PROCESSES ;
     se:label "CS2023 SE-Teamwork: Teamwork" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PROPOSED" ;
     se:node_kind "KNOWLEDGE_UNIT" ;
     se:record_version "0.1.0" ;
     se:view_ref se:VIEW-CS2023-SE .

se:NODE-07G-SEM-MEASUREMENT a se:TaxonomyNode ;
     se:created_on "2026-11-07" ;
     se:definition "The Software Engineering Measurement topic of SWEBOK Guide v4.0a KA9: development and implementation of measurement programs in software engineering organizations, presented in the chapter as following the ISO/IEC/IEEE 15939 measurement process (establish and sustain commitment, plan, perform, evaluate)." ;
     se:evidence_refs se:EVD-07G-SWEBOK-KA9-MEASUREMENT ;
     se:label "SWEBOK KA9 topic 6: Software Engineering Measurement" ;
     se:lifecycle_status "PROPOSED" ;
